  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-08-15T22:01:57.773Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "A description of each of the 6 attached photos, in order to explain the issue, from left to right 1-6 respectively:\n\n1. Left hand pre-update and at rest, note how the tip of the index finger is slightly raised above the others, which is expected to reflect your actual finger positioning IRL.\n\n2. Right hand pre-update and with the trigger pulled to activate the \"fist\" gesture, note how the index finger is now pulled down and aligned with the other fingers, which is expected to reflect your actual finger positioning IRL.\n\n3. Left hand post-update and at rest in the middle of the trigger, note that the index finger in an expected position, slightly raise above the others.\n\n4. Left hand post-update and with the trigger pulled to activate the \"fist\" gesture, note that the index finger sunken into the palm of the hand.\n\n5. Right hand post-update and at rest at the base of the trigger on the controller (closest to the tip of the controller), note that the index finger is now sunken into the hand slightly and further than it had been on the other hand when the trigger was pulled, this further exaggerates that same trigger pull while the trigger finger is placed in this position. \n\n6. Right hand post-update and at rest at the very farthest tip of the trigger on controller, note that the index finger is now placed higher and further out of alignment with the other fingers than expected.\n\nAlso shown in the 6th photo is how, with some finger placements on the controller, the rest of the fingers will be pulled too far and clip into the hand as well.\n\nI have also experienced issues with my pinkie finger not aligning with the rest of the fingers while at rest or while the trigger is pulled, unless I stretch my finger further down the grip, which was not an issue pre-update and is not a feasible solution for myself and other people with smaller hands that don't cover the entire grip.\n\nAll of this is incredibly immersion breaking and makes it very uncomfortable (at least for me) to look at your own and other people's hands.\n\nThe legacy hand IK is also not working properly to reflect how the hand should be situated to represent the IK pre-update, but that has been mentioned in another Canny post.\n\n(Sorry for the separated paragraphs that make this post long, I wanted to make it easier to read for everyone who has issues reading plain text that is grouped closely together, like myself.)",
